<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abhai Singh of Marwar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1702">1702</a>–<a href="/years/1749">1749</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Abhai Singh of Jodhpur</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abhai Singh was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rathore">Rathore</a> maharaja of Marwar, ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jodhpur">Jodhpur</a> from 1724 to 1749. He came to the throne after the murder of his father, Ajit Singh, and served the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughals</a> as governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a> in the 1730s. His brothers established a new Rathore line at Idar in 1728.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abhai-singh-of-marwar.jpg" alt="Abhai Singh of Marwar" width="220" height="310" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Abhai_Singh.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
